## Guardrails

- Git identity must be `simplex5` — verify before any commit or push.
- Never push to `upstream` (the friend's repo). Pushes go to `origin` only, and only when the user asks.
- Never commit `database/` (brain ticket DB) — it is gitignored; keep it that way.
- Respect the existing code style and structure — this is inherited code; prefer minimal,
  surgical changes over rewrites until the codebase is well understood.
- yfinance is unauthenticated scraping-adjacent — don't add loops that hammer it; keep
  request volume near what the app already does.
- Run `pytest tests/` before reporting any change to signals/indicators/backtesting as done.

*(Add new guardrails as mistakes happen. Keep this under 10 items.)*
